<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37478" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξοιδα</span></b> , pf. in pres.
		sense, plpf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξῄδη</span> as impf., <i><span class="en">
			S.
			<u>Ant.</u>
			460
		</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
			<u>Tr.</u>
			988
		</span></i> (lyr.): 
			Ep.
		
		inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξίδμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.332
				</span></i>
			:—<i>know thoroughly, know well,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				129
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				95
			</span></i>, etc.: with part. agreeing with the subject, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξοιδ᾽ ἔχουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ἀνὴρ ὤν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OC</u>
					567
				</span></i>
			; with the object, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. σε οὐ ψιλὸν
				ἥκοντα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1028
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ph.</u>
				79
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				407
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφ᾽ ἡμῶν οὐδὲν ἐξειδώς</span>”
				<i>having learnt,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>OT</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧν γ᾽ ἂν ἐξειδὼς
			κυρῶ,</span> as if it were an Adj., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				399
			</span></i>: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>El.</u>
				222
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.</div>
